<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>2.3.1: Finding Connections between Graphs and Equations</item>
  <item>2.3.2: Checking Solutions in Systems
    <list>
      <item>2.3.2: Self Check</item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>2.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.3.3: Solving Equations Using Substitution
    <list>
      <item>2.3.3: Self Check</item>
    </list>
    <list>
      <item>2.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>2.3.4: Solving More Equations</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 2.3.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>Graphing technology</item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their
  own device.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for
    these words and notice their use and meanings.</item>
  <item>Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link></item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
